WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:03.290
- Our first Wildflower of the Season Two,

00:00:03.290 --> 00:00:06.360
is well, out of this world.

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:11.060
Diana Trujillo is a
NASA Aerospace Engineer

00:00:11.060 --> 00:00:12.950
working on the Perseverance Rover,

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:17.380
which is currently searching
for signs of life on Mars.

00:00:17.380 --> 00:00:21.220
We caught up with her at the
NASA Jet Propulsion Laboratory,

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:24.650
just outside of LA in
Pasadena, California.

00:00:24.650 --> 00:00:28.720
And I know that you're going
to be as blown away by her

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:31.220
and her backstory as we were.

00:00:31.220 --> 00:00:34.010
There's a lot about kind of school

00:00:34.010 --> 00:00:37.990
in the theme of this show,
so take a look at this.

00:00:37.990 --> 00:00:40.310
Hello everybody, we are coming to you

00:00:40.310 --> 00:00:44.250
from a very special location.

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:46.320
We're on Mars.

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:49.390
Well, actually we're on
the simulation of Mars

00:00:49.390 --> 00:00:54.290
and we are here with our
Wildflower, Diana Trujillo.

00:00:54.290 --> 00:00:57.780
It's your backstory
that really inspires me.

00:00:57.780 --> 00:01:01.110
You came here from Columbia at 17.

00:01:01.110 --> 00:01:01.943
- That's correct.

00:01:01.943 --> 00:01:04.700
- What was your fear
and what was your dream?

00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:08.300
- My fear there was, am I
gonna be able to eat today.

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:10.660
Am I gonna be able to
have the shelter today?

00:01:10.660 --> 00:01:11.830
Where am I gonna sleep.

00:01:11.830 --> 00:01:14.280
In my dream at the same
time was to survive.

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:16.330
When I was in Columbia,
and I was thinking that,

00:01:16.330 --> 00:01:18.720
everything around me was chaotic.

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:22.020
Looking at the sky was the
place where I found myself.

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:24.780
- What a beautiful thing to turn to

00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:27.940
in such pain and chaos and fear.

00:01:27.940 --> 00:01:32.500
And the payoff is we're here at NASA.

00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:34.166
(Diana laughs)

00:01:34.166 --> 00:01:36.140
You are a leading engineer.

00:01:36.140 --> 00:01:39.570
- I channelize my grandma,
my great-grandma, my mom,

00:01:39.570 --> 00:01:43.470
and I realized, they really
gave up their education

00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:44.700
for the children.

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:47.250
It is time for me to honor
what they did for me,

00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:50.180
and also to show the men in my family,

00:01:50.180 --> 00:01:53.180
that women can do more
than what they think.

00:01:53.180 --> 00:01:54.917
I remember myself asking,

00:01:54.917 --> 00:01:57.780
"What's the hardest thing
that a human can do?"

00:01:57.780 --> 00:01:59.250
And then thinking, "I'm gonna do that."

00:01:59.250 --> 00:02:00.270
- Oh my gosh.
(Diana laughs)

00:02:00.270 --> 00:02:02.940
That's so cool, I can't even handle it.

00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:05.870
- I end up going to University of Florida,

00:02:05.870 --> 00:02:08.550
and I told one of my professors,
I want to work for NASA.

00:02:08.550 --> 00:02:11.460
He suggested that I
apply to the NASA Academy

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:14.300
and I remember looking at the
applications and I'm concerned

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:16.710
because you know, English
is my second language,

00:02:16.710 --> 00:02:19.420
and at that point I was not gonna send it,

00:02:19.420 --> 00:02:21.710
and so my roommate send it for me.

00:02:21.710 --> 00:02:24.480
18 students got selected
for the NASA Academy,

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:27.420
I was the only Latin woman in that class.

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:29.490
- I'm convinced that
there are literal angels

00:02:29.490 --> 00:02:31.700
because that teacher and your roommate

00:02:31.700 --> 00:02:33.330
took that bold step for you.

00:02:33.330 --> 00:02:35.780
So I just want to encourage people in life

00:02:35.780 --> 00:02:39.890
to help encourage other
people to take bold steps.

00:02:39.890 --> 00:02:44.890
You've made it now to NASA,
what is your position right now?

00:02:45.380 --> 00:02:47.810
- With Perseverance we're trying to answer

00:02:47.810 --> 00:02:50.040
if there was life in the past.

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:52.686
- It seems like the party's over in Mars.

00:02:52.686 --> 00:02:53.678
(Diana laughs)

00:02:53.678 --> 00:02:55.580
Like everybody's kind
of resting and chilling.

00:02:55.580 --> 00:02:56.413
- That's right.

00:02:56.413 --> 00:02:58.281
- The Coachella is not happening on Mars.

00:02:58.281 --> 00:02:59.114
(Diana laughs)

00:02:59.114 --> 00:03:01.530
What happens if you realize, okay,

00:03:01.530 --> 00:03:03.280
there was life here before?

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:06.650
- My personal hope is maybe
we'll change our perspective

00:03:06.650 --> 00:03:08.730
as humans as to how we treat each other

00:03:08.730 --> 00:03:10.650
and how we treat our home planet.

00:03:10.650 --> 00:03:13.750
- I mean, doing "E.T."
when I was six years old

00:03:13.750 --> 00:03:16.200
is not the impetus for my next comment,

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:18.750
but I am convinced
we're not the only ones.

00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:21.240
- I agree. (laughs)

00:03:21.240 --> 00:03:23.567
- This is one of the Rovers
that we use to understand

00:03:23.567 --> 00:03:25.440
certain things on mobility.

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:26.760
Mikey, would you mind.

00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:27.830
- So this is Scarecrow.

00:03:27.830 --> 00:03:29.420
- Why did you name it Scarecrow,

00:03:29.420 --> 00:03:30.364
is it a "Wizard of Oz" reference?

00:03:30.364 --> 00:03:32.030
- It is a "Wizard of Oz"
reference. (Drew claps)

00:03:32.030 --> 00:03:32.863
- Ha.
- So, the brains.

00:03:32.863 --> 00:03:33.696
- There's no place like home.

00:03:33.696 --> 00:03:35.588
That's the big theme
of our show this year.

00:03:35.588 --> 00:03:36.740
(TV static)

00:03:36.740 --> 00:03:39.470
- This is our sister Rover,

00:03:39.470 --> 00:03:42.260
the spare parts of the
actual Perseverance Rover.

00:03:42.260 --> 00:03:45.420
- This is the dry run to make
sure you're getting it right

00:03:45.420 --> 00:03:47.600
so that when you execute it on Mars,

00:03:47.600 --> 00:03:49.916
you have had your practice
and you're going in

00:03:49.916 --> 00:03:52.330
really knowing.
- What's gonna happen.

00:03:52.330 --> 00:03:56.070
- Exactly. (musical swooshing)

00:03:56.070 --> 00:03:57.544
Wow.

00:03:57.544 --> 00:03:58.377
(digital beeping)

00:03:58.377 --> 00:04:00.290
This is my war games fantasy.

00:04:00.290 --> 00:04:01.123
(woman laughs)

00:04:01.123 --> 00:04:03.270
Oh my God, I thought I
was about to go through

00:04:03.270 --> 00:04:04.800
a hole in the floor but it's not.

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:07.820
- No, this is the center
of the universe. (laughs)

00:04:07.820 --> 00:04:11.290
From here we command
lots and lots of missions

00:04:11.290 --> 00:04:12.960
that are going to different planets,

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:14.900
Mars missions, and beyond.

00:04:14.900 --> 00:04:18.650
This is my baby, the robotic arm on Mars.

00:04:18.650 --> 00:04:22.130
- Diana, you are making it your mission

00:04:22.130 --> 00:04:26.950
to include the Latinx community.

00:04:26.950 --> 00:04:29.410
What is it that you
would like to accomplish?

00:04:29.410 --> 00:04:32.780
- I want to take down the expectation

00:04:32.780 --> 00:04:35.530
of what women are supposed to be doing.

00:04:35.530 --> 00:04:39.230
I have two kids, I'm married,
and I'm also doing this,

00:04:39.230 --> 00:04:41.010
so you get to do it all.

00:04:41.010 --> 00:04:45.020
- I don't think that there
is a bigger inspiration

00:04:45.020 --> 00:04:47.930
out there than you, Diana.

00:04:47.930 --> 00:04:49.000
Thank you.

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:53.313
You are truly my hero. (laughs)

00:04:54.515 --> 00:04:57.098
(upbeat music)

